JailJawn is a learning project that collects public data. Two notes on
using it, and no warranties on any of it.

THE DATA (data/, raw/, legacy/, census.csv, feed.xml, feed.json and
latest.json) is dedicated to the public domain under CC0 1.0:
https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/
The figures were published by the Philadelphia Department of Prisons and
collected with the city's permission; nobody claims copyright over them
here. Do anything you like with them. If you find them useful, a mention
of "JailJawn by Stanley Griggs II, github.com/ST215/JailJawn" is
appreciated, but it is not a condition. The data is provided as is,
without warranty of any kind: it is what the city published on each day,
captured as faithfully as the scraper could manage.

